cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these datasets, please cite them using the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: "huspm-datasets: quantitative sequence databases for high-utility sequential pattern mining"
abstract: >
  Generated internal quantities and external profits for seven sequence
  databases of the public SPMF dataset collection, used across several
  high-utility sequential pattern mining studies so that each measures on
  exactly the same bytes. The SPMF sequences are not distributed here: a
  script joins the released quantities and profits with the SPMF files the
  user downloads, and checks the SPMF files and the assembled databases
  against pinned SHA-256 checksums. The quantities and profits were generated
  by SPMF_Converter with a fixed seed and a per-file random stream.
